  "notes": "Warren J. Smith, Modern Lens Design, 2nd ed., Figure 21.13, p. 408. Book: EFL -4997, BFL 1032, NA 0.0246 (F/100.0), HFOV 8.25, VL 337.98, infinite conjugate. Wavelengths 10, 8, 13 um as in the book (primary first). Glass: GERMA entered as 4.003228 (constant index inside the book's rounded 4.003, chosen to match the book's EFL; the telescope is so nearly afocal that its EFL follows the fourth decimal of the germanium index). The book does not mark the stop; it is placed at surface 1, the front surface. Infrared materials come from the Zemax INFRARED catalog; the book lists their indices at the primary wavelength from older data, so small differences in EFL are expected. Afocal 5x telescope. As in the book (Afo 1000, MAG 5), an ideal lens of focal length 1000 follows it so it can be evaluated at a finite focus. EPD = |EFL|/F# (49.97). The book's VL 337.98 leaves out the 32.390 air space before the ideal lens. HFOV is read from the field plots. Discrepancy with the book: with germanium at 4.00323 the EFL matches, but the paraxial image lies about 1000 behind the ideal lens instead of the book's 1032.",
